* A row of Pascal's triangle. Each binomial coefficient comes from the one
* before it: c becomes c·(n-k)/(k+1).
1.1 Type n, k, c in form 1.
1.2 Set c = c·(n-k)/(k+1).
Form 1:
__ choose __ is ____
Set n = 10.
Set c = 1.
Do part 1 for k = 0(1)n.
10 choose  0 is    1
10 choose  1 is   10
10 choose  2 is   45
10 choose  3 is  120
10 choose  4 is  210
10 choose  5 is  252
10 choose  6 is  210
10 choose  7 is  120
10 choose  8 is   45
10 choose  9 is   10
10 choose 10 is    1
